  {
    "statement": "Using environmentally-sensitive material, such as ECOncrete or rock, often alongside added habitat features, supported fish species absent from standard surfaces.",
    "citations": [
      "3470"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Using environmentally-sensitive material had mixed effects on fish abundance, depending on the species.",
    "citations": [
      "3470"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Transplanting or seeding organisms like oysters onto structures increased the combined richness and diversity of invertebrate and fish species.",
    "citations": [
      "3471"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Transplanting or seeding organisms onto structures altered the community composition.",
    "citations": [
      "3471"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "The overall combined abundance of invertebrates and fish did not increase from transplanting or seeding organisms, with effects varying among species.",
    "citations": [
